research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_TRANSMUTATION.title=Transmutation Protocol
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_TRANSMUTATION.text.0=The transmutation records describe something far bolder than changing one substance into another. The tablets propose opening the inner signature of a finished item and altering selected properties without destroying the whole. Their calculations repeatedly invoke a Primordial Pearl, a Nether Star, and an Eldritch Curiosity. Comparing these structures with a Transmutation Core formed in the well should provide control over this directed alteration.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_TRANSMUTATION.text.1=The §lTransmutation Protocol§r accepts an item into the Riftonomicon's central stream. Prisms may be placed around it, while each §lPrismatic Subsystem§r opens one additional position, up to four. Touching the structure with a Transmutation Core begins the rite and consumes the core; Paradoxum and a supplied current of energy sustain what follows.<BR>For weapons and tools, Ignis favours damage, Aer attack speed, and Terra durability reserve. Every matching prism adds 25% to the preferred result; Aqua provides no preference for this group. Armour chooses among the installed prisms: Ignis grants armour, Aqua armour toughness, Aer fall protection, and Terra durability. A uniform set makes the result certain.<BR>For focus lenses, Ignis raises power, Terra duration or burn duration, Aer radius, and Aqua forks. A uniform set always changes its matching setting when that setting exists; a mixed set leaves the choice to the system.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_TRANSMUTATION.text.2=The §lTransmutation Protocol§r accepts an item into the Riftonomicon's central stream. Prisms may be placed around it, while each §lPrismatic Subsystem§r opens one additional position, up to four. Touching the structure with a Transmutation Core begins the rite and consumes the core; Paradoxum essentia and a current of §lImpetus§r sustain what follows.<BR>For weapons and tools, Ignis favours damage, Aer attack speed, and Terra durability reserve. Every matching prism adds 25% to the preferred result; Aqua provides no preference for this group. Armour chooses among the installed prisms: Ignis grants armour, Aqua armour toughness, Aer fall protection, and Terra durability. A uniform set makes the result certain.<BR>For focus lenses, Ignis raises power, Terra duration or burn duration, Aer radius, and Aqua forks. A uniform set always changes its matching setting when that setting exists; a mixed set leaves the choice to the system.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_CREATION.title=Creation Protocol
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_CREATION.text.0=The creation records describe a way to turn the Riftonomicon into a machine that remembers not an item's appearance, but the law by which it exists. A Primordial Pearl and Nether Star are again required to reconstruct the design, though its final key is an Ancient Curiosity. A Creation Core must serve as the blank foundation upon which the scanning arrays can gradually form a stable sigil of the studied item.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_CREATION.text.1=With the §lCreation Protocol§r installed, place a Creation Core at the Riftonomicon's centre and identical samples of the item in its four outer scanning arrays. The protocol opens one array; every §lScaling Subsystem§r opens another, up to four. Each active array requires its own supply of Paradoxum and energy. These fuel the scan, while the Creation Core becomes the substance of the sigil. Formation takes three complete ritual passes: the blank changes after each, becoming a finished sigil after the third. Additional arrays accelerate research, but every sample remains vulnerable to instability.<BR>Place the completed sigil in the upper socket of a §lRift Extractor§r. An extractor within 16 blocks binds to the nearest Riftonomicon and assembles the recorded item layer by layer, drawing Paradoxum and energy through it. The protocol supports two extractors; each Scaling Subsystem adds two more, to a maximum of eight. Damageable items require several passes to reach full durability, and a redstone signal pauses the extractor.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_CREATION.text.2=With the §lCreation Protocol§r installed, place a Creation Core at the Riftonomicon's centre and identical samples of the item in its four outer scanning arrays. The protocol opens one array; every §lScaling Subsystem§r opens another, up to four. Each active array requires its own supply of Paradoxum essentia and §lImpetus§r. These fuel the scan, while the Creation Core becomes the substance of the sigil. Formation takes three complete ritual passes: the blank changes after each, becoming a finished sigil after the third. Additional arrays accelerate research, but every sample remains vulnerable to instability.<BR>Place the completed sigil in the upper socket of a §lRift Extractor§r. An extractor within 16 blocks binds to the nearest Riftonomicon and assembles the recorded item layer by layer, drawing Paradoxum and Impetus through its upper supply node. The protocol supports two extractors; each Scaling Subsystem adds two more, to a maximum of eight. Damageable items require several passes to reach full durability, and a redstone signal pauses the extractor.

research.ARCANEEAR.ta_addendum_ear_band=Experiments with the Clockwork Mind have borne fruit. The calibrated Arcane Ear is now capable of hearing an entire range of notes. And the higher the note, the stronger the signal I was able to obtain.
research.BASEELDRITCH.ta_addendum_voidtile_from_seed=The seeds are highly volatile and malleable. By selecting the proper essentia, I was able to transform them into a proper building material.

research.TA_GOLEMCRAFT.title=Golem Craftsmen
research.TA_GOLEMCRAFT.text.intro=Research consumes nearly all my attention. And how irritating it is when, in the middle of the process, I have to run back to a workbench just to make yet another trinket. Fortunately, my latest studies in golemancy may solve this once and for all.
research.TA_GOLEMCRAFT.text.main=Excellent. I have managed to create a mechanism upon which all crafting tasks can be successfully delegated. The improved workbench is capable of requesting the necessary materials from the warehouse on its own. One only needs to place the proper instructions inside. The workbench is sensitive to redstone signal strength, and this determines which instructions it will follow. It still requires a supply of Fabrico essentia to function, and the more complex the task, the more of it will be needed.

research.TA_GOLEMDELIVERY.title=Order Ready for Delivery
research.TA_GOLEMDELIVERY.text.intro=The Stock Seal handles some of the work adequately, but it is time to think of something more functional.
research.TA_GOLEMDELIVERY.text.main=After studying the Hungry Chest and the Stock Seal more closely, I assembled a Greatwood Crate. Its principle is quite simple: I can place several Delivery Orders into the crate, and by supplying a redstone signal of a certain strength, the golems will execute the corresponding order. <BR>Once the order is fulfilled, the crate will move all items into adjacent storage while preserving the order specified in the request. If no storage is nearby, it will simply place them beneath itself.

research.TA_GOLEMCRAFT_AD.title=Arcane Upgrade
research.TA_GOLEMCRAFT_AD.text.intro=The Golem Workbench has proven itself productive and reliable. It is time to find a way to adapt this mechanism for arcane transformations as well.
research.TA_GOLEMCRAFT_AD.text.main=With a few components for vis control and by replacing the fuel with Auram essentia, the workbench becomes capable of transforming raw materials into complex thaumaturgical devices.

research.TA_GOLEM_MIRRORS.title=Golems and Mirrors
research.TA_GOLEM_MIRRORS.text.0=Golems are excellent at finding and delivering items, but there is no limit to perfection. To restock supplies, I still have to walk to the warehouse and wait while the golems rummage through chests on my behalf. Yet I have an idea how this might be improved.
research.TA_GOLEM_MIRRORS.text.1=I did it! The solution was so simple—Mirrors. I managed to create a device that can serve as the basis for an entire logistics network. <BR>The §lMirror Manipulator§r works in tandem with the §lWarehouse Librarian§r. Shift-right-click the Manipulator and then right-click the Librarian, and they will know of one another. The Librarian records all items from nearby storages marked with Provision Seals; simply specify the desired item and quantity, and the order will be put into action. Golems will bring everything needed to the Manipulator, and it will send the items onward to the requester. However, the Manipulator must contain a mirror through which the items pass to the Librarian. <BR>The Manipulator destabilizes itself while operating, which has a negative effect upon the surrounding aura. But if a source of Ordo essentia is kept nearby, this side effect can be avoided.

research.TA_GOLEM_SEAL_TUNING.title=Additional Tuning
research.TA_GOLEM_SEAL_TUNING.text.intro=Seals reveal an unpleasant flaw when a system is scaled up: the “right” golem is not always the one that answers a task. The seals announce their work faithfully, yet leave the choice of worker to chance. This illogic should be correctable; I already have ideas for teaching a seal to distinguish its intended hands.
research.TA_GOLEM_SEAL_TUNING.text.main=I have managed to imbue the Warehouse Bell with the ability to tell golems which seals they should serve. This additional tuning does not override a seal's other requirements or the golem's own limitations, but it does allow suitable workers to be assigned precisely.<BR>To configure a whitelist, hold the Warehouse Bell and shift-right-click the desired seal. The bell will remember it and begin to glint. Then right-click golems with that bell: the first click adds a golem to the selected seal's whitelist, while a second click removes it. Another thaumaturge's seal cannot be altered.<BR>While the list is empty, every otherwise suitable golem may answer the seal. Once even a single golem is listed, only the named workers may accept its tasks. Right-clicking the air with the bell clears its selected link, but does not erase the whitelist already assigned to the seal.

research.TA_GOLEM_INTEGRATION.title=Advanced Transportation
research.TA_GOLEM_INTEGRATION.text.0=Experience has shown that the Manipulator is incapable of maintaining a connection with several consumers at once. A core powered by a primordial pearl is simply not strong enough to sustain the levitation of more than one mirror.
research.TA_GOLEM_INTEGRATION.text.1=I not only managed to solve the issue of a limited number of mirrors, but also developed additional functionality for the Manipulator. The Mirror Stabilizer is a device that reduces the load levitating mirrors places upon the core, and it scales quite well—each stabilizer can support up to two additional mirrors. The Mirror Beacon is a new tool for creating supply channels. To function, it must be placed above a Golem Workbench and linked to a Manipulator whose structure contains a Computing Core. Computing Cores allow the Manipulator to fulfill raw material orders for Golem Workbenches, and each one supports two beacons. One important note: due to their construction, the Manipulator’s upgrade blocks must be connected in alternating order—Core, then Stabilizer, then Core, and so on.

research.TA_GOLEMCONTROLER.title=Proper Management
research.TA_GOLEMCONTROLER.text.intro=There is often utter chaos in the warehouse. I need a device capable of organizing the way golems work with resources.
research.TA_GOLEMCONTROLER.text.main=Success! The Task Distributor is ready! <BR>Now the Mirror Manipulator is capable not only of processing orders in parallel, but of understanding exactly how many golems are assigned to it. First, connect the Distributor to the Manipulator, then Shift-right-click the Distributor and right-click a Golem. From then on, only that Golem will work for the Manipulator. <BR>The Distributor consumes one mathematical slot of the Manipulator for each Golem assigned to it.

research.TA_CRAFTCONTROLER.title=A Well-Laid Plan
research.TA_CRAFTCONTROLER.text.intro=Sometimes I have to keep too much in mind: whether the warehouse has the materials I need, whether there are enough components for a craft. This must be automated.
research.TA_CRAFTCONTROLER.text.main=I have created a device that solves several problems at once. First, if I order something and the warehouse lacks a required material, the order will not be placed. Second, if the shortage can be covered by crafting from materials already available, the warehouse will be restocked as needed and the Mirror Manipulator will perform the required crafts on its own.

research.TA_AUTOORDERS.title=Inspect and Order
research.TA_AUTOORDERS.text.intro=Resource supplies always demand attention, and it is impossible to keep track of everything. But if the warehouse gains an Auditor, life becomes easier.
research.TA_AUTOORDERS.text.main=The Revision Piedestal is another helper for warehouse work. It has two modes: §l"Order"§r and §l"Comparator"§r. The piedestal connects to a §lMirror Manipulator§r and can hold a single item. <BR>In §l"Comparator"§r mode, it emits a redstone signal with strength proportional to the number of that item in the warehouse. The threshold can be adjusted with Shift-left-click, and if an arcane or otherworld stone is placed beneath it, the threshold is increased further. <BR>In §l"Order"§r mode, the piedestal does not emit redstone; it receives it. When it receives a redstone signal, it places a crafting order equal to the configured threshold. The craft result will be sent back into this piedestal, and if a golem seal is placed below it, the items will be extracted safely.

research.TA_GOLEMINFUSION.title=Remote Infusion
research.TA_GOLEMINFUSION.text.intro=Infusion at the matrix takes a great deal of time and demands constant supervision. Yet I have begun to wonder whether this process might be automated.
research.TA_GOLEMINFUSION.text.main=The §lInfusion Controller§r is a block capable of performing operations with the Infusion Matrix without my direct involvement, provided it is supplied with §lInfusion Instructions§r.<BR>The Controller must be bound to the pedestals and the runic matrix it is meant to operate. Shift-right-clicking the Controller begins the linking process, right-click is used to bind pedestals—the §lcentral pedestal§r must be linked first—and Shift-right-click is used to bind the matrix. <BR>Each placement of an item upon a pedestal consumes Alienis essentia. <BR>The ritual may be started by a redstone signal.

research.TA_BOTANY.title=Otherworld Agriculture
research.TA_BOTANY.text.0=Abyssblooms—flowers found in surface anomalies—lead me to believe that alchemy and infusion may help transform them into a new and useful form of crop. All that remains is to determine how.
research.TA_BOTANY.text.1=Chorus Fruits turned out to be excellent vessels for the mutable nature of Abyssblooms. The resulting Mutable Seeds cannot take root in ordinary soil, but I managed to create Experimental Soil specifically for this botanical marvel. Water also proved useless as irrigation. Yet Purifying Salts Solution and Liquid Death both gave positive results. Depending on irrigation and the state of the surrounding aura, the seeds produce different fruits.
research.TA_BOTANY.text.2=After gathering the harvest, I returned to the laboratory. Feeding the plants with Purifying Salts Solution produced two results: Fruits of Pure Mind. They can ripen fully if the surrounding aura is rich in vis, or remain unripe if the aura is poor. Feeding them with Liquid Death always produces fruits saturated with Flux. I have managed to find a use for every harvest, and the fruits of Mutable Seeds are themselves valuable alchemical ingredients.

research.TA_ANOMALY.title=Distortion Anomalies
research.TA_ANOMALY.text.0=While closing rifts I found something clearly not of this world, alongside the usual void seeds. It feels as if the collapse tears out a fragment of another nearby world; perhaps in other dimensions I will find something rarer still. <BR>I have also begun to notice strange disturbances in the aura, as though my research is leaving an irreparable scar upon this world. It seems I have underestimated the influence of Flux upon the aura, and the consequences may become irreversible. <BR>No anomalies are visible in the lands where I currently reside, but what lurks in the far corners of this world and its dark caves remains to be discovered.
research.TA_ANOMALY.text.1=My fears were justified. The Flux I create slowly but surely distorts the aura of this world; the process is so severe that it affects everything from the deepest caverns to the very surface. Materials extracted from anomalies are unique and highly suited to alchemy and infusion. But my samples have run out, and I have managed to develop only purification methods. I must find more.
research.TA_ANOMALY.text.2=Anomalies have firmly taken root in this world. They appear chaotically whenever several distorted currents of aura collide. After conducting further experiments, I have developed transformation formulas for all of these materials.

research.TA_ELDRITCH_CONSTRUCTION.title=Ancient Constructions
research.TA_ELDRITCH_CONSTRUCTION.text.0=Within the ruins of the anomalies, stone and metal are joined as though they had never been separate materials. There are scarcely any seams, and the masonry still contains alien energy after untold ages. Ordinary materials cannot endure such strain, but Dark Jasper behaves differently.<BR>Given the proper inner structure, it could become more than a building material: it could serve as the foundation of an entire family of ancient mechanisms. I need only discover how readily it will permit itself to be altered once formed.
research.TA_ELDRITCH_CONSTRUCTION.text.1=After countless failed specimens, I have produced a sufficiently universal Ancient Construction. Its Dark Jasper matrix retains its shape, carries magical currents, and remains stable enough to become part of far more elaborate devices.<BR>The true discovery came later. The construction eagerly accepts Rift Amber, Amethyst, and Diamond into its substance. The gems do not merely fasten to its surface—the material reshapes itself around them, as though a place had always been waiting for each one.<BR>Every variety gains a magical resonance of its own. The plain, Amber, Amethyst, and Diamond Ancient Constructions are therefore not decorative forms of the same base, but distinct structural elements suitable for supports, conduits, and essential components of future mechanisms.

research.TA_AURA_BOOSTER.title=Void Pylon
research.TA_AURA_BOOSTER.text.0=Otherworld Quartz and Abyssalite Crystals, when stored together, begin to emit a faint magical glow. There may be potential in this.
research.TA_AURA_BOOSTER.text.1=Abyssalite interacts with essentia in a fascinating way, especially Auram essentia, but when I passed essentia through a cluster of crystals I nearly blew myself sky-high. In its pure state Abyssalite is unstable; Dark Jasper and Rift Amethyst helped solve this problem by stabilizing the vis flow emitted by the Abyssalite. <BR>The result of my research is the Void Pylon. This structure safely enriches the aura with additional vis. The pylon requires Auram essentia to function—simply place a jar nearby. Its efficiency can be improved further by installing a Primordial Pearl into its base.
research.TA_AURA_BOOSTER.text.2=Abyssalite interacts with essentia in a fascinating way, especially Auram essentia, but when I passed essentia through a cluster of crystals I nearly blew myself sky-high. In its pure state Abyssalite is unstable; Dark Jasper and Rift Amethyst helped solve this problem by stabilizing the vis flow emitted by the Abyssalite. <BR>The result of my research is the Void Pylon. This structure safely enriches the aura with additional vis. The pylon requires Auram essentia to function—simply place a jar nearby. Its efficiency can be improved further by installing a Primordial Pearl into its base. <BR>If Impetus is directed through it instead of essentia, its efficiency grows even greater.

research.TA_GEM.title=Void Charms
research.TA_GEM.text.0=The gems drawn from the Rift only appear lifeless. Beneath the thaumometer each reveals a pattern almost as intricate as that of a Primordial Pearl, though fractured and restless.<BR>My attempts to channel this power directly ended in ruined instruments and a most instructive explosion. Void metal, however, does not reject the alien radiance. It accepts the gem, closes around it, and conducts its resonance onward. Fashioned into a small setting, it may bind the gem's power to armor without permitting that power to touch its wearer directly.
research.TA_GEM.text.1=The calculations were correct. Void metal holds the gem like a lens and compels the force within to flow across the armor's surface. I have named these inlays §lVoid Charms§r. One stone produces a modest but stable effect; two resonate, while four close a complete circuit.<BR>§lAmber§r answers the passage of vis through a caster's gauntlet. Depending on purity, each stone strengthens spells by 5, 6, or 7%. Two ambers raise focus power, duration, radius, and forks by one further step. Four prevent focus recovery from exceeding two seconds, though the aura demands another 4 vis for every second stolen from the wait.<BR>§lAmethyst§r seeks to receive a blow in its wearer's stead and transforms ordinary runic shielding into §lRunic Wards§r. Every 4 shielding points form one ward: 8 points become two wards, 12 become three, and so forth. Each amethyst improves the wards' damage absorption efficiency by 2, 3, or 4%. When a single strike destroys more than two wards, a pair begins an emergency restoration and gradually returns four wards. Each restored quarter of a ward costs 8 vis, and the restoration cannot recur for 25 seconds. A circuit of four reveals its true nature whenever any single ward breaks completely—for the next 1.5 seconds, only one fifth of the damage passing through the remaining wards reaches the wearer.<BR>§lDiamond§r renders a weapon's movement almost weightless. Stones of differing quality increase attack speed by 3, 4, or 5%, though the total gain cannot exceed 20%. A pair drives a Flux pulse through the victim on every third strike, its power equal to the sum of every diamond tier worn. A complete circuit draws 6 vis from the aura with each hit. Upon gathering 36 vis it births a combat firefly for five seconds; the creature seeks nearby foes and assails them with triple volleys of Flux at power 8.

research.TA_RIFTONOMICON.title=Riftonomicon
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON.text.0=The cleared tablets of the Anomalous Archive proved to be fragments of a single description for an elaborate construction binding matter, space, and the energy of the Rift. Much of the text still resists deciphering, while several diagrams appear to contradict one another or deliberately conceal essential stages of assembly.<BR>Even so, enough fragments remain for me to attempt a reconstruction of the central structure. I will need Ancient Constructions capable of enduring its weight and magical strain, Rift Amethysts, and a far deeper theoretical understanding of the Eldritch.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON.text.1=I have managed to embody a fragment of the knowledge recovered from the tablets of the Anomalous Archive. I have named the resulting construction the §lRiftonomicon§r. Its structure unites numerous interconnected nodes, though the purpose of many of them remains a mystery.<BR>I still do not understand the exact principles by which it operates. Some components begin working before they receive a command, while currents within the structure occasionally travel against every expected direction. For now, only one fact is certain: the Riftonomicon feeds upon Paradoxum essentia. Everything else must be learned through cautious experimentation.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON.text.2=I have managed to embody a fragment of the knowledge recovered from the tablets of the Anomalous Archive. I have named the resulting construction the §lRiftonomicon§r. Its structure unites numerous interconnected nodes, though the purpose of many of them remains a mystery.<BR>I still do not understand the exact principles by which it operates. Some components begin working before they receive a command, while currents within the structure occasionally travel against every expected direction. For now, I know only that the Riftonomicon feeds upon Paradoxum essentia and Impetus energy. How it binds those forces together, and what it may transform them into, remains to be discovered.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_NAVIGATION.title=Navigation Protocols
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_NAVIGATION.text.0=One pattern repeats throughout the knowledge recovered from the cleared archive: a network of Crimson Cult portals reduced to coordinates, directions, and points of passage. Until now, using such a system would have meant entrusting myself to a device built for an entirely unknown purpose.<BR>The Riftonomicon, however, may serve as a safe intermediary. If taught to recognize directions and sustain links between locations by itself, it could command the cult's portals without surrendering control to the will behind them. To reconstruct this fragment of technology, I must examine every component from which the well forms a Navigation Core and compare their properties with the recovered records.
research.TA_RIFTONOMICON_NAVIGATION.text.1=The calculations were correct. The §lNavigation Protocol§r turns the Riftonomicon into the control node of a portal network, while §lSpatial Subsystems§r increase the number of destinations the construction can maintain at once. The protocol must be installed in one of the Riftonomicon's empty nodes; compatible subsystems may then be placed into the remaining nodes.<BR>A §lNavigation Stone§r stores a pair of linked locations. Shift-right-clicking the first portal records it, while right-clicking a second portal binds the two sides and opens the passage. The same stone can thereafter operate the pair in either direction.<BR>To give a bound stone to the Riftonomicon, simply throw it into the void at the base of the construction. The protocol will draw it in and place it among the floating markers. Right-clicking a marker commands the Riftonomicon to open the nearest suitable portal toward its recorded destination. Shift-right-clicking a marker with an empty hand retrieves that specific stone; shift-right-clicking the Riftonomicon itself with an empty hand retrieves the most recently installed one.

research.TA_RIFT_ENCHANTMENT.title=Otherworld Enchantments
research.TA_RIFT_ENCHANTMENT.text.0=The Charms have proven that the properties of Void Gems may be directed, yet the setting remains only an intermediary. The stone slowly exhausts itself, and the power within never truly becomes part of the item.<BR>Infusion offers another path. Rather than holding the gem outside the object, I may dissolve its magical pattern into the object itself—weaving an alien property between the bonds already present. This will demand a subtler balance than ordinary enchantment. A mistake may do more than shatter the matrix; it may convince the item that it has always been something else.
research.TA_RIFT_ENCHANTMENT.text.1=I have isolated three stable patterns. They bear little resemblance to ordinary enchantments: the item does not wear them upon its surface, but seems to remember qualities it never possessed.<BR>§lCharging Runes§r arise from the resonance of Rift Amber. Applied to an item capable of storing vis, they slowly gather scattered energy and replenish its charge.<BR>Rift Amethyst suggested another means of weaving §lRunic Shielding§r. This ritual adds one point of protection to armor or an amulet and, unlike the method already known to me, always demands the same price. The matrix does, however, grow increasingly reluctant to accept another layer: its base instability is 6 and rises by one for every two shielding points already applied. The old method remains useful—I may now choose between a growing price and a growing risk.<BR>The pattern of a Rift Diamond proved much like a tautened thread. §lOtherworldly Lightness§r strips weapons and tools of a portion of their imagined weight, allowing them to move with unsettling ease.

