research.TA_ANOMALY_ARCHIVE_INFO.title=Anomalous Archive
research.TA_ANOMALY_ARCHIVE_INFO.text=<IMG>thaumicattempts:textures/research/anomaly_archive.png:0:0:256:211:.5</IMG>Deep beneath the familiar lands I found a place that clearly does not belong here. Colossal tablets stand among ancient columns, covered in a cipher unlike any language known to me. Yet some of the symbols feel disturbingly familiar, as though their meaning already lingers at the edge of my thoughts.<BR>Much of the writing lies buried beneath growths of anomalous stone. If I am to reach the knowledge hidden below, I must first clear the tablets carefully with a pickaxe—and avoid damaging whatever has endured here for untold ages.
research.TA_ANOMALY_LABORATORY_INFO.title=Anomalous Laboratory
research.TA_ANOMALY_LABORATORY_INFO.text=<IMG>thaumicattempts:textures/research/anomaly_laboratory.png:0:0:256:143:.5</IMG>Strange laboratories hide both upon the heights and in the deepest hollows of the Nether. Their makers are long gone, yet the central well still lives: a dense transmutative liquid shimmers in its basin and reacts to objects cast into it.<BR>It does not merely dissolve matter. It compels several objects to merge into a single new form. A successful transmutation consumes some of the liquid, but the well slowly restores what was lost, as though drawing strength from the Nether itself.
research.TA_ANOMALY_MONOLITH_INFO.title=Anomalous Monolith
research.TA_ANOMALY_MONOLITH_INFO.text=<IMG>thaumicattempts:textures/research/anomaly_monolith.png:0:0:256:175:.5</IMG>Among the desolate islands of the End, rings of ancient stone hang over the void with a silent monolith at their heart. It draws in traces of impossible energy, condenses them into Paradoxum essentia, and casts that essence toward the anomalous pedestals around it.<BR>An empty pedestal is not enough—it needs a vessel capable of surviving contact with paradox. The Rift Amethyst is such a vessel. Its crystal structure accepts Paradoxum and slowly becomes saturated without shattering beneath the pressure of that alien force.
tile.thaumicattempts.infusion_matrix_upgrade.name=Secondary Runes
item.thaumicattempts.infusion_matrix_upgrade.name=Secondary Runes
research.TA_SECONDARY_RUNES.title=Infusion: Secondary Runes
research.TA_SECONDARY_RUNES.text.intro=The Infusion ritual is one of the foundations of thaumaturgy. Its course is relatively stable and its outcome sufficiently predictable, provided that every necessary precaution is observed. Yet my understanding has long since outgrown familiar methods. It is time to introduce newer knowledge into this art as well.
research.TA_SECONDARY_RUNES.text.main=I have created §lSecondary Runes§r—auxiliary patterns able to guide the work of a Runic Matrix. They may be placed directly over any of the matrix's six faces. This interference greatly hastens the ritual, though the time gained is paid for with additional instability.<BR>Each installed set of Secondary Runes forms one more parallel channel for the Runic Matrix. It can therefore draw several different kinds of essentia at once, then move several required items from their pedestals simultaneously. The more faces covered by runes, the swifter the Infusion becomes—and the more closely the stability of the entire structure must be watched.
